<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ x.title }} — Thalamus experiment {{ x.slug }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ x.standfirst }}">
<style>{{ css }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="masthead">
  <p class="eyebrow">Thalamus · experiment {{ x.slug }}</p>
  <h1>{{ x.title }}</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">{{ x.standfirst }}</p>
  <div class="byline">
    <span>{{ x.provenance.generated_at }}</span>
    <span>snapshot <code>{{ x.provenance.snapshot }}</code></span>
    <span>seed <code>{{ x.provenance.seed }}</code></span>
    <span>code <code>{{ x.provenance.git_ref }}</code></span>
  </div>
</header>

{% if x.verdict %}
<div class="verdict {{ x.verdict_kind }}">
  <span class="verdict-kind">{{ x.verdict_kind }}</span>
  <p>{{ x.verdict }}</p>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if x.stats %}
<div class="stats">
  {% for s in x.stats %}
  <div class="stat">
    <p class="stat-label">{{ s.label }}</p>
    <p class="stat-value">{{ s.value }}</p>
    {% if s.interval %}<p class="stat-interval">{{ s.interval }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if s.null %}<p class="stat-null">{{ s.null }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if s.note %}<p class="stat-note">{{ s.note }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="preregistration">What was committed to before the data was seen</h2>
<div class="registration">
  <dl>
    <dt>Question</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.question }}</dd>
    <dt>Hypothesis</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.hypothesis }}</dd>
    <dt>Endpoint</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.endpoint }}</dd>
    <dt>Falsifier</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.falsifier }}</dd>
    <dt>Stopping rule</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.stopping_rule }}</dd>
    {% if x.registration.registered_at %}
    <dt>Registered</dt><dd>{{ x.registration.registered_at }}{% if x.registration.registered_ref %} · <code>{{ x.registration.registered_ref }}</code>{% endif %}</dd>
    {% endif %}
  </dl>
</div>

{% for section in x.sections %}
<h2{% if section.anchor %} id="{{ section.anchor }}"{% endif %}>{{ section.title }}</h2>
{{ section.body }}
{% endfor %}

<h2 id="reproducibility">Reproducibility</h2>
<p>Every number and figure above regenerates from a pinned graph state and a seed.
Nothing here was computed against the live graph, which moves whenever a session ends.</p>
<pre><code>{{ x.provenance.command }}</code></pre>
<p>The snapshot is <code>{{ x.provenance.snapshot }}</code>
({{ x.provenance.snapshot_vertices }} vertices, {{ x.provenance.snapshot_edges }} edges,
sha256 <code>{{ x.provenance.snapshot_sha256[:16] }}</code>), served read-only by
<code>thalamus snapshot --serve</code>.</p>

<ul class="checklist">
{% for item in x.checklist %}
  <li>
    <span class="mark mark-{{ 'yes' if item.state == 'yes' else ('no' if item.state == 'no' else 'na') }}">{{ '✓' if item.state == 'yes' else ('✗' if item.state == 'no' else '–') }}</span>
    <span>{{ item.requirement }}{% if item.detail %}<span class="check-detail">{{ item.detail }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3>What is deliberately absent</h3>
<p>The graph itself is not published. It is one operator's session history and the
evidence archive holds their transcripts verbatim — credentials, client names and
personal history included. The snapshot hash lets anyone holding the same state
verify that these numbers came from it; it does not let a stranger recompute them
from scratch, and no wording here should imply otherwise.</p>

<footer class="colophon">
  <p>Thalamus · experiment {{ x.slug }} · generated {{ x.provenance.generated_at }} from
  <code>{{ x.provenance.git_ref }}</code>. Checklist after Pineau et al.,
  <em>Improving Reproducibility in Machine Learning Research</em>, JMLR 22(164), 2021.</p>
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
